      "detail": {
        "body": "**Version**\ncommit ad8c59add6a1988d8c327fb3358beeeae3bbb5cd\n\n**Platform**\nmacos\n\n**Description**\nHi team, one weird issue that I found when I tried to forget permits from a closed semaphore: it's reopened again.\nI think there're a few acceptable behaviors:\n- Reject the forget operation by returning status\n- Decrement the permit count, but it should be kept closed\n\nI tried this code:\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn forget_permits_on_closed_semaphore_must_stay_closed() {\n    let s = Semaphore::new(10);\n    s.close();\n\n    assert!(s.is_closed());\n    assert_eq!(s.available_permits(), 10);\n    assert_eq!(s.forget_permits(4), 4);\n\n    // BUG: after forget_permits, the semaphore should still be closed,\n    // but forget_permits clears the CLOSED bit from the atomic permits counter.\n    assert!(\n        s.is_closed(),\n        \"semaphore should still be closed after forget_permits\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(s.available_permits(), 6);\n}\n```\n",
        "closedAt": "2026-04-08T08:00:00Z",
